WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.134
The Chinese military

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:01.901
says a

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:03.003
US spy plane

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:05.038
deliberately intruded into a Navy

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:07.040
training area last week in the South

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:07.907
China Sea

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:09.275
and is urging Washington

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:11.344
to restrain its troops.

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:13.413
This is a response to this video

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:14.681
released by the US.

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:16.216
It shows a Chinese fighter

00:00:16.216 --> 00:00:16.916
jet cutting

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:19.719
right in front of an American spy plane

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:21.354
which had to fly through

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:22.689
the wake turbulence.

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:24.758
US officials called the fighter's move

00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:26.593
unnecessarily aggressive.

00:00:26.593 --> 00:00:27.360
CNN's Natasha

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.129
Bertrand is at the Pentagon.

00:00:29.129 --> 00:00:31.064
The US says the fighter jet

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:33.700
was in international airspace.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:34.601
Well, China is saying

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:36.336
this is an act of provocation.

00:00:36.336 --> 00:00:37.837
It is important to understand

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:39.372
the context here

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:40.473
wider tensions

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:42.375
that have been brewing for a while.

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:43.376
But where are we in

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:44.677
terms of what both sides

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:45.745
are saying to each other?

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:47.514
Yeah.

00:00:47.614 --> 00:00:49.349
So we actually just heard from US

00:00:49.349 --> 00:00:50.083
Secretary of State

00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:52.786
Antony Blinken, who spoke about this

00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:53.853
to reporters,

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:54.487
telling them

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:55.055
that he does

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:56.489
believe that the Chinese pilot in

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:58.358
this instance was acting very dangerously

00:00:58.358 --> 00:00:59.692
and that the US aircraft

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:01.694
was operating in international airspace.

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:03.663
But really underscoring

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:04.130
the fact

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:06.132
that this is exactly why the US wants

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:06.466
to keep

00:01:06.466 --> 00:01:07.200
those military

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.301
to military channels

00:01:08.301 --> 00:01:09.402
open with the Chinese

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:12.439
to avoid this kind of confrontation

00:01:12.439 --> 00:01:12.872
and something

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:13.206
of course

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:14.974
that could lead to a dramatic escalation

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:15.975
between the two countries.

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:17.043
And he's saying that

00:01:17.043 --> 00:01:18.178
because just this week

00:01:18.178 --> 00:01:19.712
the US Defense Secretary,

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:20.346
Lloyd Austin

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:22.082
tried to set up a meeting

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:23.416
with his Chinese counterpart

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:24.584
and that was summarily

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:26.019
rejected by the Chinese.

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:27.020
One of many meetings

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:28.721
that the US has proposed in recent months

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:29.823
that the Chinese

00:01:29.823 --> 00:01:30.690
have rebuffed

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:31.991
as a result of this heightening

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:33.560
tensions between the US and China

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:35.361
stemming from, for example.

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:35.829
Former House

00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:36.963
Speaker Nancy Pelosi's

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:38.498
visit to Taiwan last year,

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:39.599
the incident where the U.S.

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:40.400
shot down

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:41.668
a suspected Chinese spy

00:01:41.668 --> 00:01:42.836
balloon earlier this year,

00:01:42.836 --> 00:01:45.338
and other episodes where the US has been

00:01:45.338 --> 00:01:47.073
operating over the South China Sea

00:01:47.073 --> 00:01:47.941
in a way

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:49.442
that China perceives

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:51.544
as violating its own territory.

00:01:51.578 --> 00:01:53.313
Now of course the US does not

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:54.147
accept that.

00:01:54.147 --> 00:01:55.014
They do not believe

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:56.382
that the South China Sea

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:57.951
is controlled by the Chinese.

00:01:57.951 --> 00:01:59.252
But all of this

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:01.354
is really contributing to this.

00:02:01.421 --> 00:02:03.189
This tension between the U.S.

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:03.623
and China.

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:05.492
And China is pushing back,

00:02:05.492 --> 00:02:06.759
of course, this morning

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:07.594
with the foreign ministry

00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:08.461
releasing a statement

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:09.596
saying that the US

00:02:09.596 --> 00:02:10.063
was acting

00:02:10.063 --> 00:02:11.131
in a provocative way

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:12.298
and the Chinese military

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:13.867
releasing a separate statement

00:02:13.867 --> 00:02:14.634
saying that the US

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:15.668
had actually interfered

00:02:15.668 --> 00:02:17.237
in their training exercises

00:02:17.237 --> 00:02:19.572
So all of this really underscoring

00:02:19.572 --> 00:02:20.306
for the US

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:22.175
why it's important to have this dialog

00:02:22.175 --> 00:02:24.344
so that as two major

00:02:24.344 --> 00:02:25.712
obviously military powers,

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:27.881
they avoid some kind of collision

00:02:27.881 --> 00:02:29.215
that could then

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:30.016
spark a broader

00:02:30.016 --> 00:02:31.784
conflict between the two countries.

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:32.819
This incident comes

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:34.220
at a very sensitive time.

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:36.289
So let's expand the conversation now

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:37.290
with CNN military

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:38.958
analyst General Wesley Clark.

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:39.959
He is a former

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:42.061
supreme allied commander of NATO's.

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:43.429
General, thank you so much

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:44.631
for being with us.

00:02:44.631 --> 00:02:46.633
At the core of this incident

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.868
is the dispute between China

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:51.004
and the United States over the South

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:51.671
China Sea.

00:02:51.671 --> 00:02:53.139
China says this happened

00:02:53.139 --> 00:02:55.008
over their training ground.

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:56.042
The United States says

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:57.410
this was international waters.

00:02:57.410 --> 00:02:58.678
I'm wondering what you make

00:02:58.678 --> 00:02:59.846
of that dispute

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:03.283
Well, I think it's very

00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:04.751
important for the United States

00:03:04.751 --> 00:03:05.785
to continue

00:03:05.785 --> 00:03:06.486
to insist

00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:08.655
that this is international waters.

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:10.423
Something like a third of the world's

00:03:10.423 --> 00:03:11.858
commerce goes through the South

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:12.926
China Sea.

00:03:12.926 --> 00:03:14.494
That's not China's

00:03:14.494 --> 00:03:15.962
territorial waters

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:18.331
under the Law of the Sea convention.

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:20.500
It is something that they declared was

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:23.236
a nice so-called nine dash line.

00:03:23.236 --> 00:03:24.837
That was some government

00:03:24.837 --> 00:03:25.338
road up

00:03:25.338 --> 00:03:27.240
from China in 1948,

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.342
and they've suddenly seized on it.

00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:31.644
This has gone on for several years.

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:33.246
They built up the atolls,

00:03:33.246 --> 00:03:34.981
they put air bases on these atolls

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:36.783
after they promised they wouldn't.

00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:37.951
They armed them with air

00:03:37.951 --> 00:03:38.685
defense missiles,

00:03:38.685 --> 00:03:40.220
after they promised President Obama

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:41.721
they wouldn't do that.

00:03:41.721 --> 00:03:43.990
And so we're continuing to assert

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:45.158
freedom of navigation,

00:03:45.158 --> 00:03:47.193
the seas and freedom

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:50.230
to do air reconnaissance in the skies.

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:52.332
And we must continue to insist on this.

00:03:53.166 --> 00:03:53.666
Obviously,

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:55.702
one of many points of contention

00:03:55.702 --> 00:03:56.736
between the two powers,

00:03:56.736 --> 00:03:57.770
but perhaps

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:59.372
the most likely to lead

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:01.040
to a dangerous escalation and.

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:03.543
Right, because as we saw in this video,

00:04:04.043 --> 00:04:04.744
the surveillance

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:06.646
plane encounters turbulence.

00:04:06.646 --> 00:04:08.715
If there's any kind of miscommunication

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:10.817
or miscalculation

00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:12.085
there could be a serious incident

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:15.488
That's right.

00:04:15.488 --> 00:04:17.123
It could cause an incident.

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:19.559
And it's happened in the past.

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:21.127
Some 20 years ago,

00:04:21.127 --> 00:04:21.861
an American

00:04:21.861 --> 00:04:22.862
reconnaissance plane

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:23.696
had its wing

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:26.165
clipped by a Chinese fighter.

00:04:26.165 --> 00:04:27.800
It had to make a forced landing

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:29.869
in Chinese territory.

00:04:29.869 --> 00:04:32.405
The Chinese got an intelligence bonanza

00:04:32.405 --> 00:04:33.373
out of that.

00:04:33.373 --> 00:04:35.108
I'm sure our river joint crews

00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:37.043
are very well aware of this incident.

00:04:37.043 --> 00:04:38.745
They're very cautious.

00:04:38.745 --> 00:04:40.280
And if anything were to happen,

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:40.613
of course,

00:04:40.613 --> 00:04:41.514
the number one thing is

00:04:41.514 --> 00:04:43.082
protect the intelligence

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:44.817
collection information

00:04:44.817 --> 00:04:46.953
that's on board that rivet joint

00:04:46.953 --> 00:04:49.122
that has to be protected at all cost.

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:50.823
But this is the nature

00:04:50.823 --> 00:04:51.991
of the intelligence game.

00:04:51.991 --> 00:04:53.126
We've got to fly there.

00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:54.560
We've got to get their radars

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:55.828
to alert us.

00:04:55.828 --> 00:04:57.830
We've got to pick up the emissions

00:04:57.830 --> 00:04:58.965
from those radars

00:04:58.965 --> 00:04:59.699
to understand

00:04:59.699 --> 00:05:00.600
what's there and what

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:01.768
the threat might be.

